PART 2: UNDERSTANDING VANILLA JAVASCRIPT

================================================================================

What is Vanilla JavaScript?

Vanilla JavaScript means using plain JavaScript without additional frameworks or libraries.

Characteristic          | Meaning
------------------------|-----------------------------------------------
Pure JavaScript         | JavaScript without UI frameworks/libraries
No React/Vue/Angular    | Uses browser APIs directly
DOM Manipulation        | JavaScript directly accesses HTML elements
Event Handling          | Uses APIs such as addEventListener()
State Management        | Application data is managed manually

Example: Vanilla JavaScript
// Vanilla JavaScript - Direct DOM manipulation

const button =
  document.getElementById('myButton');

const paragraph =
  document.getElementById('myParagraph');

button.addEventListener('click', () => {
  paragraph.textContent = 'Button was clicked!';
});

Code Explanation
Code / Method                     | Purpose
----------------------------------|------------------------------------------
getElementById('myButton')        | Finds the button element
getElementById('myParagraph')     | Finds the paragraph element
addEventListener('click', ...)    | Listens for the user's click
paragraph.textContent = ...       | Directly changes paragraph content

Flow
USER CLICKS BUTTON
        ↓
Event Listener Executes
        ↓
Find/Use DOM Element
        ↓
Change textContent
        ↓
Browser Displays New Text


