Problem 1: Complex State Management
What is State?

State is data whose current value helps determine what the user sees or how the application behaves.

Examples:

State                    | Example Value
-------------------------|-------------------------
User logged in?          | true / false
Selected date            | May 10
Shopping cart items      | 5
Search query             | "React"
Selected filter          | "completed"

The Challenge

In a complex application:

Multiple pieces of data must be tracked.
Data may be needed by different parts of the application.
UI must stay synchronized with the data.
When data changes, the relevant UI must update.
User actions may cause state changes.
Dependencies between data and UI can become difficult to manage manually.
Real-World Example: Calendar App

Imagine building an application such as a calendar.

User Selects May 10
        ↓
Search Events for May 10
        ↓
Display Events
        ↓
User Clicks an Event
        ↓
Display Event Details
        ↓
User Edits Event
        ↓
Update Data
        ↓
Update Calendar Display
        ↓
Keep UI and Data Synchronized


With Vanilla JavaScript, developers may need to manually:

Task
------------------------------------------------
Track selected date
Fetch events for selected date
Update displayed events
Handle user interactions
Update event information
Keep application data and UI synchronized
Handle edge cases


As application size increases, coordinating these responsibilities manually can become difficult.

