Problem 2: Direct DOM Manipulation

================================================================================

What is the DOM?

DOM = Document Object Model

The DOM is the browser's object/tree representation of an HTML document.

It allows JavaScript to access and modify HTML elements.

DOM Characteristic       | Meaning
-------------------------|-------------------------------------------
Representation           | Represents the HTML document
Structure                | Elements form a tree
Access                   | JavaScript can locate elements
Modification             | JavaScript can change elements
Connection               | Connects JavaScript with document content

Example HTML
<html>
  <body>

    <h1>My App</h1>

    <p id="message">
      Hello
    </p>

    <button id="myButton">
      Click Me
    </button>

  </body>
</html>

DOM Tree
Document
└── html
    └── body
        ├── h1
        │   └── text: "My App"
        │
        ├── p
        │   ├── id: "message"
        │   └── text: "Hello"
        │
        └── button
            ├── id: "myButton"
            └── text: "Click Me"


