Problem 3: DOM Traversal and Manipulation

================================================================================

What is DOM Traversal?

DOM traversal means accessing and navigating elements in the DOM tree.

It can include:

Operation           | Description
--------------------|------------------------------------------
Finding             | Locate an element
Parent Navigation   | Move from child to parent
Child Navigation    | Access children
Sibling Navigation  | Access neighboring elements
Querying            | Search for matching elements

Vanilla JavaScript Example
// Find the button
const button =
  document.getElementById('myButton');

// Find the paragraph
const paragraph =
  document.getElementById('message');

// Find the body
const body =
  document.querySelector('body');

// Find all paragraphs
const allParagraphs =
  document.querySelectorAll('p');

// Navigate to parent
const parent =
  paragraph.parentElement;

// Navigate to children
const children =
  body.children;

Code Explanation
Code / Property                | Purpose
-------------------------------|------------------------------------------
getElementById('myButton')     | Finds element with id="myButton"
querySelector('body')          | Finds first matching body element
querySelectorAll('p')          | Returns matching paragraph elements
paragraph.parentElement        | Gets paragraph's parent element
body.children                  | Gets child elements of body


Manual traversal requires the developer to understand and work with the document structure directly.

