Problem 5: State and DOM Can Become Tightly Coupled

================================================================================

What Does "Coupled" Mean?

Coupling means different pieces of application logic depend closely on each other.

Strong coupling can make code harder to modify, test, and maintain.

Vanilla JavaScript Example
let count = 0;

const button =
  document.getElementById('incrementBtn');

const display =
  document.getElementById('countDisplay');

button.addEventListener('click', () => {

  count = count + 1;

  display.textContent = count;
});


Here:

State             | count
DOM Element       | display
State Update      | count = count + 1
DOM Update        | display.textContent = count


The developer must keep count and the displayed value synchronized manually.

Example Bug
count = count + 1;

// Forgot:
// display.textContent = count;


Possible situation:

Actual State
count = 5

Displayed UI
count = 3

Result
STATE ≠ UI

Main Problem
State Changes
      ↓
Developer Must Remember
      ↓
Update Corresponding DOM
      ↓
If Forgotten
      ↓
STATE AND UI OUT OF SYNC


