Solution 4: Reusable Components

================================================================================

React allows UI behavior and presentation to be placed in reusable components.

React Example
function MyButton({ label, onClick }) {

  return (
    <button onClick={onClick}>
      {label}
    </button>
  );
}


Reuse it:

<MyButton
  label="Click Me"
  onClick={handleClick}
/>

<MyButton
  label="Submit"
  onClick={handleSubmit}
/>

<MyButton
  label="Cancel"
  onClick={handleCancel}
/>


The same component is reused with different values and behavior.

Vanilla JavaScript Equivalent
const button1 =
  document.createElement('button');

button1.textContent =
  'Click Me';

button1.addEventListener(
  'click',
  handleClick
);

const button2 =
  document.createElement('button');

button2.textContent =
  'Submit';

button2.addEventListener(
  'click',
  handleSubmit
);

Comparison
Vanilla JavaScript          | React
----------------------------|------------------------------------
Create elements manually    | Define reusable component
Set text manually           | Pass label as prop
Attach listeners manually   | Pass event handler as prop
Repeated setup              | Reuse same component


