PART 5: VANILLA JS VS REACT

================================================================================

Aspect             | Vanilla JavaScript        | React
-------------------|---------------------------|-----------------------------
State Management   | Manually coordinated      | State APIs such as useState
DOM Updates        | Developer manipulates DOM | React manages DOM commits
UI Style           | Often imperative          | Declarative/component-based
Code Complexity    | Can grow significantly    | Structured through components
Maintainability    | Harder as app grows       | Often easier for complex UIs
Reusability        | Must design manually      | Component reuse is core pattern
Performance        | Depends on implementation | Reconciliation optimizes updates
Learning Curve     | Core language/browser API | Adds JSX, components, hooks, etc.
Debugging          | Browser/code tooling      | React + browser tooling
Collaboration      | Depends on architecture   | Component structure can help
Scalability        | Possible with discipline  | Designed well for complex UIs


Important:

Vanilla JavaScript is NOT inherently "bad" or always slow.

React becomes especially valuable when:
→ UI complexity grows
→ Many pieces of state exist
→ Components must be reused
→ State and UI must remain synchronized
→ Many developers work on the UI


