Concept 3: Virtual DOM / Reconciliation

================================================================================

The Virtual DOM is commonly used to describe React's in-memory representation of UI elements.

Simplified flow:

STATE CHANGES
     ↓
NEW RENDER OUTPUT
     ↓
REACT COMPARES/RECONCILES
     ↓
DETERMINES REQUIRED CHANGES
     ↓
REAL DOM UPDATED

Concept          | Purpose
-----------------|------------------------------------------
Render Output    | Describes desired UI
Reconciliation   | Determines what changed
DOM Commit       | Applies required changes to browser DOM
Keys             | Help identify list items between renders


================================================================================

Concept 4: Coupling

================================================================================

Coupling describes how strongly different parts of an application depend on one another.

Aspect         | Vanilla JS Risk              | React Approach
---------------|------------------------------|-------------------------------
State          | Can be separate from DOM     | UI rendered from state
DOM Changes    | Often manually coordinated   | React commits UI changes
Data Flow      | Can become difficult to trace| Component/state structure
Maintenance    | Dependencies can spread      | Components improve organization


Easy memory:

VANILLA JS

Change State
     +
Remember DOM Update


REACT

Change State
     ↓
Render UI from Current State


